# Secrets and local config — never in the repo
#
# The patterns are BROAD on purpose, and the reason is a real scar: on
# 01/08/2026 an `api/.env.bak-2026-08-010343` slipped into the your main website repo
# — the whole .env, with Stripe, Firebase and FLEET_CRED_KEY inside — because
# the rules only covered the exact names someone had imagined.
#
# Rule: anything that STARTS with .env and isn't the example stays out.
# Un-ignoring a false positive is trivial; un-publishing a key is not.
.env
.env*
api/.env
api/.env*
**/.env*
# The example DOES go in the repo: variable names only, no values.
!.env.example
!api/.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Firebase Admin SDK keys — NEVER in the repo
*service-account*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
sa-key*.json

# Dependencies and build artifacts
node_modules/
web/dist/

# System
.DS_Store

# graphify knowledge graph — local artifact
graphify-out/
.graphify_*

# The spikes symlink api/'s node_modules instead of duplicating it.
# The `node_modules/` pattern above doesn't match a symlink.
spike/*/node_modules
.worktrees/
